WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.992
Winn's fingers flew.

2
00:00:06.993 --> 00:00:11.114
The little cube in his hands twisted and turned.

3
00:00:11.115 --> 00:00:19.419
Bright, colorful squares moved at a rapid pace.

4
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:24.682
"Oh, a Rubik's Cube puzzle!" said Anika.

5
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:28.913
"I just got one for my birthday."

6
00:00:28.914 --> 00:00:32.965
"I'm trying to solve it quickly," said Winn.

7
00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:37.009
He stopped turning the cube and studied it for a moment.

8
00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:43.612
Then he turned the top layer clockwise and studied it again.

9
00:00:43.613 --> 00:00:48.368
Finally he sighed and set the puzzle on the table.

10
00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:52.865
"I wish I'd invented the Rubik's Cube," he said.

11
00:00:52.866 --> 00:00:55.678
"Then I could solve it easily!"

12
00:00:55.679 --> 00:01:02.310
Anika laughed. "I'm not so sure about that.

13
00:01:02.311 --> 00:01:08.323
It took the inventor a month to solve it the first time!"

14
00:01:08.324 --> 00:01:13.676
"Really?" said Winn. "Who invented it?"

15
00:01:13.677 --> 00:01:17.723
"A man named Erno Rubik," said Anika.

16
00:01:17.724 --> 00:01:21.838
"He was an architecture professor."

17
00:01:21.839 --> 00:01:28.215
Winn scratched his head. "Why did he invent a toy?"

18
00:01:28.216 --> 00:01:33.864
"Rubik didn't think of the cube as a toy at first," said Anika.

19
00:01:33.865 --> 00:01:39.842
"He invented it in 1974 to test out a design idea.

20
00:01:39.843 --> 00:01:49.607
But then he realized people really liked playing with the cube.

21
00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:54.213
He decided to manufacture and sell it."

22
00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:59.155
"He sold a lot of them, right?" asked Winn.

23
00:01:59.156 --> 00:02:06.162
"Rubik's Cube was extremely popular in the 1980s," said Anika.

24
00:02:06.163 --> 00:02:09.182
"Today it's still popular.

25
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:14.955
In fact, it's one of the world's top-selling toys."

26
00:02:14.956 --> 00:02:23.477
Winn grinned. "Well, someday I'm going to be the world's speed-cubing champion!"

27
00:02:23.478 --> 00:02:27.373
"Oh, really?" asked Anika.

28
00:02:27.374 --> 00:02:30.770
"Yep," said Winn.

29
00:02:30.771 --> 00:02:35.694
"There are speed-cubing competitions all over the world.

30
00:02:35.695 --> 00:02:40.328
The first world championship was held in 1982.

31
00:02:40.329 --> 00:02:45.260
People try to solve the Rubik's Cube as fast as they can.

32
00:02:45.261 --> 00:02:49.837
And there are different types of competitions too.

33
00:02:49.838 --> 00:02:53.352
Some people solve it with one hand.

34
00:02:53.353 --> 00:02:56.334
Others solve it blindfolded.

35
00:02:56.335 --> 00:03:00.486
Some people even solve it with their feet!"

36
00:03:00.487 --> 00:03:04.615
Winn picked up the cube and started twisting it again.

37
00:03:04.616 --> 00:03:11.432
"A lot of people can solve it in less than ten seconds," he said.

38
00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:15.470
"How fast are you?" asked Anika.

39
00:03:15.471 --> 00:03:18.643
Winn gave a sheepish grin.

40
00:03:18.644 --> 00:03:24.478
"Actually, I haven't solved it at all yet."

41
00:03:24.479 --> 00:03:28.607
"Don't feel bad," said Anika.

42
00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.875
"It's not easy to solve.

43
00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:36.485
There are billions of ways a Rubik's Cube can be scrambled."

44
00:03:36.486 --> 00:03:41.946
Winn put the cube down again.

45
00:03:41.947 --> 00:03:45.436
"This is taking me forever!"

46
00:03:45.437 --> 00:03:49.098
Anika picked up the cube and started twisting it.

47
00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:56.116
"A Rubik's Cube can always be solved in fewer than twenty moves."

48
00:03:56.117 --> 00:03:59.592
"Impossible," said Winn.

49
00:03:59.593 --> 00:04:05.461
"I'm serious," said Anika as she continued to move the sides around.

50
00:04:05.462 --> 00:04:13.202
"Thirteen, fourteen, fifteen, sixteen . . . done!"

51
00:04:13.203 --> 00:04:16.156
Anika held out the Rubik's Cube.

52
00:04:16.157 --> 00:04:32.738
Winn's eyes grew wide. "You solved it!"

